{"term":"cheat","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:8d002bb08c8810d59c","definition":"To violate rules in order to gain, or attempt to gain, advantage from a situation.","example":"My brother flunked biology because he cheated on his mid-term.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cheat#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d011c649f4c701fd66","definition":"To be unfaithful to one's spouse or partner; to commit adultery, or to engage in sexual or romantic conduct with a person other than one's partner in contravention of the rules of society or agreement in the relationship.","example":"My husband cheated on me with his secretary.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["step out on"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"intransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cheat#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:2a1c275d1c25691a84","definition":"To avoid a seemingly inevitable thing.","example":"He cheated death when his car collided with a moving train.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cheat#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b758aa2a49264da3a4","definition":"To deceive; to fool; to trick.","example":"My ex-wife cheated me out of $40,000.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["rook","blench","lirt","burn","beguile"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wi